WEBVTT

00:43.458 --> 00:48.292
[distorted vocalizing]

00:56.667 --> 00:59.667
[water dripping]

01:16.292 --> 01:17.500
[metal clanging]

02:00.917 --> 02:01.917
[electricity crackling]

02:02.583 --> 02:06.125
[machinery whirring]

02:18.625 --> 02:21.250
[faint chatter on radio]

02:24.542 --> 02:26.833
[gasps] Fuck me.

02:26.917 --> 02:28.417
[Siberian] Hey.

02:30.750 --> 02:33.292
Who does surgery on a crashing ship?

02:35.042 --> 02:37.250
I don't think they died in the crash.

02:38.667 --> 02:39.833
Look at their faces.

02:41.583 --> 02:43.167
Looks like suffocation.

02:44.292 --> 02:47.750
Or cabin depressurized, maybe.
Suddenly they're breathing space.

02:47.833 --> 02:50.000
No, see the blue lips?

02:50.583 --> 02:51.833
Some kind of toxin.

03:02.958 --> 03:04.125
Whoa.

03:04.208 --> 03:08.167
He had some kind of foreign bodies
lining his GI tract.

03:08.250 --> 03:09.417
There's an incident code.

03:09.500 --> 03:11.083
1562.

03:16.333 --> 03:18.333
Looks like they're gone now.

03:19.042 --> 03:20.417
Okay, come on.

03:20.500 --> 03:22.208
We're search and rescue.

03:22.292 --> 03:24.292
Let forensics Agatha Christie this shit.

03:34.625 --> 03:36.375
Search and rescue!

03:46.625 --> 03:48.000
[Hermit] Rashidi.

03:49.833 --> 03:51.958
1562, foreign bodies…

03:52.458 --> 03:54.667
-Yeah, you said that.
-[electricity crackling]

03:54.750 --> 03:55.833
It's bad.

03:56.917 --> 03:57.917
Bad how?

03:58.958 --> 04:00.958
Wait, what do you mean foreign?

04:03.042 --> 04:04.042
Alien.

04:06.292 --> 04:09.417
[sighs] This day just
gets better and better.

04:58.167 --> 04:59.375
Up or down?

05:00.125 --> 05:03.917
[Rashidi] Chief said to go down,
so we're going down.

05:05.417 --> 05:06.417
Let's move.

05:07.000 --> 05:08.000
[Siberian] Hey.

05:10.167 --> 05:14.000
[Marcy] Well, I really like Wendy because
I know that she's like a big sister to me,

05:14.083 --> 05:15.708
like one I never had,

05:15.792 --> 05:21.833
and I know that everyone is really kind
and I love all the children.

05:21.917 --> 05:25.625
[child 1] I'm really looking forward
to not being sick anymore.

05:25.708 --> 05:27.125
It's really bad.

05:27.208 --> 05:28.792
I really hate it.

05:28.875 --> 05:33.458
[child 2] I can't wait to be so smart
and so intelligent.

05:34.458 --> 05:36.208
I could solve any problem.

05:36.292 --> 05:39.333
I'm excited…

05:39.417 --> 05:41.042
I'm scared, but it's…

05:41.125 --> 05:43.833
I think it'll be worth it. [laughs]

05:44.333 --> 05:45.583
[Boy Kavalier] Such potential.

05:46.083 --> 05:48.958
[chews] People say that
about children. Hmm?

05:49.667 --> 05:50.917
What they could be.

05:51.708 --> 05:54.292
You're talking about achievement.

05:55.083 --> 05:57.125
But it's about becoming.

05:57.708 --> 06:00.458
Teaching them to be their best selves.

06:03.833 --> 06:05.000
Uh-huh.

06:07.042 --> 06:09.625
[bites, chews]

06:09.708 --> 06:13.625
The fear with
artificial intelligence is that,

06:14.125 --> 06:18.042
you know,
we will build a brilliant machine

06:18.125 --> 06:21.833
that will build an even smarter machine,
so on…

06:22.333 --> 06:26.750
Until so long us. [chews]

06:26.833 --> 06:29.583
What we're doing here, you and me,

06:30.292 --> 06:32.667
is exploding human potential.

06:33.875 --> 06:36.792
Then we'll see what they build
before the machines ruin everything.

06:37.542 --> 06:40.500
It's an intelligence race.

06:40.583 --> 06:44.542
But if they don't stay human,
then what did we win?

06:45.500 --> 06:46.833
I'm serious.

06:46.917 --> 06:49.292
We did something
nobody thought was possible.

06:50.625 --> 06:53.708
-We ended death.
-Hmm.

06:54.458 --> 06:56.917
Now we have to make
their quality of life better,

06:57.000 --> 07:02.542
otherwise all we've done
is make consumers immortal.

07:04.500 --> 07:06.042
It's not about money.

07:08.292 --> 07:10.833
People always think
it's about money with trillionaires.

07:12.250 --> 07:13.417
Or ego.

07:13.500 --> 07:16.375
But you know… [stammers] …you know
what I really want?

07:17.125 --> 07:20.000
I wanna talk to somebody smarter than me.

07:20.583 --> 07:21.750
Thanks.

07:21.833 --> 07:23.208
Yeah, I mean, you're smart.

07:23.708 --> 07:25.958
[smacks lips] You're just not smarter.

07:27.292 --> 07:28.875
And Kirsh?

07:28.958 --> 07:30.167
Kirsh is information smart.

07:31.333 --> 07:34.458
Data cross-references with the musings
of every great philosopher,

07:34.542 --> 07:35.875
but that's not wisdom.

07:37.125 --> 07:40.875
For once in my life,
I want to climb to the top of the mountain

07:40.958 --> 07:46.375
and debate with someone who blows my mind.
[chomps, chewing]

07:47.625 --> 07:49.500
And you think that's the children.

07:50.958 --> 07:52.042
Maybe.

07:54.417 --> 07:57.042
At the very least, my hope is that…
[inhales sharply]

07:57.125 --> 08:01.708
…by giving Wendy
a supercomputer for a brain

08:01.792 --> 08:05.417
and training by the best geniuses
money can buy,

08:05.500 --> 08:09.292
I'll finally be able to have
an interesting fucking conversation.

08:25.708 --> 08:27.417
Did a ship really crash?

08:31.125 --> 08:33.125
Are there gonna be dead bodies?

08:33.833 --> 08:34.833
Don't…

08:36.958 --> 08:38.125
Don't think about that.

08:42.125 --> 08:43.375
What are you thinking about?

08:45.667 --> 08:46.833
It's a secret.

08:48.458 --> 08:49.458
Okay?

08:54.583 --> 08:55.667
I have a brother.

08:56.333 --> 08:59.250
And he works in the city.
He's a-a medic, like a doctor?

09:00.000 --> 09:01.292
[chuckles] And he's really good at it too.

09:01.375 --> 09:03.542
And he's down there
right now saving lives,

09:03.625 --> 09:05.583
but what if… [sighs]

09:06.125 --> 09:09.167
He's not like us, Slightly.
He's not premium.

09:09.250 --> 09:14.542
He can break and bleed and-and burn,
and I made him stay.

09:20.375 --> 09:21.625
So I'm gonna find him.

09:26.333 --> 09:28.542
My dad got a cold and died in Mumbai.

09:29.708 --> 09:32.042
And we burned him on this pyre,
which is very holy.

09:34.417 --> 09:37.125
But every night after, I worry,
what if he's not dead?

09:41.292 --> 09:43.875
And… And we burned him anyway.

09:44.917 --> 09:46.208
[Kirsh] Ready yourselves.

09:47.458 --> 09:48.458
Gear up.

09:52.458 --> 09:53.958
Don't worry. We'll find him.

09:55.208 --> 09:57.792
-Find who?
-Her brother. He's a doctor down there.

09:58.375 --> 09:59.708
Secret.

10:01.583 --> 10:03.667
-[Slightly chuckles]
-[Smee grunts]

10:05.167 --> 10:06.708
[sighs]

10:36.250 --> 10:37.542
We're gonna have to jump.

10:42.958 --> 10:44.708
-[Siberian] Fuck that.
-[Rashidi shouts]

10:46.000 --> 10:49.875
[grunts, groaning]

10:52.083 --> 10:53.250
[Hermit chuckles]

10:54.000 --> 10:55.750
[Rashidi] Si, come on.

10:57.750 --> 10:59.625
[exhales sharply] Watch this.

11:00.583 --> 11:02.167
[grunting]

11:02.250 --> 11:03.792
-[Rashidi groaning]
-[Siberian screams]

11:03.875 --> 11:05.333
-[Rashidi] Siberian!
-[Siberian grunts]

11:06.625 --> 11:07.917
[grunts]

11:09.292 --> 11:11.375
-Don't you fucking drop me.
-I got you. [grunts]

11:11.458 --> 11:12.708
[Siberian grunts]

11:12.792 --> 11:14.458
[both panting]

11:14.542 --> 11:16.167
[Siberian chuckles]

11:16.750 --> 11:18.958
-Hermit.
-[breathing heavily]

11:22.583 --> 11:23.917
Yo! Haul ass!

11:24.000 --> 11:26.250
[whispering] All right. Okay.

11:52.167 --> 11:54.583
-[Hermit] Oh, shit.
-[hisses]

11:54.667 --> 11:55.833
[creature screeches]

11:58.125 --> 12:02.375
[screaming]

12:03.292 --> 12:04.708
[screams]

12:20.708 --> 12:24.667
[gasps, breathing heavily]

12:26.667 --> 12:30.333
This is Hermit. Come in.
[breathing heavily]

12:30.417 --> 12:32.500
This is Prodigy medic Hermit. Come in.

12:33.500 --> 12:34.667
Requesting backup.

12:36.750 --> 12:40.833
I'm on the-the south elevator.
I'm heading up.

12:40.917 --> 12:43.042
There's a… [stammers] …creature,

12:43.125 --> 12:47.292
she's… [breathes heavily] …loose,
approximately eight feet tall.

12:48.542 --> 12:53.083
Armored. [breathes heavily]

12:53.167 --> 12:54.458
Does anyone read me?

13:01.250 --> 13:02.833
Fuck. Fuck.

13:06.208 --> 13:07.208
Okay.

13:09.292 --> 13:11.167
[grunting]

13:11.250 --> 13:14.500
[automated voice]
Now serving number 21801.

13:22.042 --> 13:24.125
[robot] Prodigy medic Hermit,

13:24.208 --> 13:26.958
please state the reason
for your visit today.

13:27.042 --> 13:31.750
Yeah, I'm following up
on forms I submitted on resigning.

13:31.833 --> 13:33.333
[clicks]

13:33.417 --> 13:35.625
Please stand by, Prodigy medic Hermit.

13:35.708 --> 13:37.792
The unit is reviewing your request.

13:39.042 --> 13:42.708
According to your file, you have
seven months remaining on your contract.

13:42.792 --> 13:44.125
Right.

13:44.208 --> 13:47.708
I'm asking special dispensation
on account of…

13:48.667 --> 13:53.625
Because I made a promise to my father
that I'd go back to medical school.

13:53.708 --> 13:58.375
Father: Frank J. Hermit.
Died January 16 of last year.

13:58.458 --> 14:00.542
Yeah, he was the last surviving…

14:01.417 --> 14:03.000
It's a long story.

14:03.083 --> 14:07.208
Isn't there a person I could talk to?
A human?

14:08.292 --> 14:10.458
Look, I've been wounded twice and…

14:10.542 --> 14:12.792
[Kirsh] She's watching him every day.
Sometimes two or three times.

14:12.875 --> 14:14.292
I gotta move on.

14:14.375 --> 14:15.750
I gotta keep my promise.

14:15.833 --> 14:17.833
You think it was a mistake
to give her access?

14:17.917 --> 14:19.375
[Hermit] To live up to my…

14:19.458 --> 14:20.708
I think it's distracting.

14:21.708 --> 14:23.208
It soothes her.

14:23.292 --> 14:24.625
It's favoritism.

14:25.208 --> 14:26.208
There's a spot for me.

14:26.292 --> 14:30.167
See? At school, medical school on Mars.

14:30.250 --> 14:32.125
They gave me a scholarship,

14:32.917 --> 14:34.792
but classes start next month, so…

14:37.625 --> 14:39.750
I'm the last one, okay?

14:41.167 --> 14:42.833
I have to do this now.

14:44.667 --> 14:45.792
[whirs]

14:46.458 --> 14:47.792
I have to do it now.

14:51.292 --> 14:53.500
[sighs] Have a heart.

14:57.375 --> 14:59.583
Or face my fury.

15:04.458 --> 15:05.917
[whirring]

15:09.917 --> 15:11.500
[robot] Face your furry what?

15:14.125 --> 15:15.250
What did you say?

15:16.042 --> 15:17.208
Did she just…

15:17.292 --> 15:19.333
What just happened? [typing]

15:19.417 --> 15:22.458
Uh, s-she rewrote the code somehow.

15:22.542 --> 15:24.250
She… Did we know?

15:24.333 --> 15:27.333
Did we give her that, uh, skill?

15:27.417 --> 15:30.708
Uh, she's connected to the Prodigy network
so we could monitor her settings

15:30.792 --> 15:33.667
and data streams in both directions, but
it never occurred to us that she would…

15:33.750 --> 15:34.792
[Hermit] What did you say?

15:37.333 --> 15:38.583
Did you just…

15:39.750 --> 15:42.792
Thank you, Prodigy medic Hermit.
Your request has been denied.

15:43.458 --> 15:47.208
You will complete your contractually
agreed upon time in this location.

15:47.292 --> 15:48.667
Have a productive day.

15:57.458 --> 15:59.500
[whirring]

16:05.000 --> 16:09.208
[sirens wailing]

16:12.792 --> 16:16.500
[indistinct radio chatter]

16:28.000 --> 16:31.000
[radio chatter continues]

16:31.750 --> 16:34.750
[sirens wailing continues]

16:45.917 --> 16:48.917
[buzzing]

16:57.750 --> 16:59.042
[buzzing continues]

16:59.125 --> 17:00.125
Do you hear that?

17:00.917 --> 17:02.000
What?

17:02.083 --> 17:04.875
It's like a buzzing.

17:15.958 --> 17:17.958
[buzzing]

17:23.750 --> 17:25.125
[soldiers chattering]

17:26.542 --> 17:27.625
[horn honking]

17:28.917 --> 17:30.917
Colonel Nagg, crisis response team.

17:31.000 --> 17:32.833
Kirsh, chief scientist, Prodigy One.

17:32.917 --> 17:37.792
[buzzing]

17:37.875 --> 17:38.875
This way.

17:38.958 --> 17:42.667
[sirens wailing]

17:49.750 --> 17:53.458
[Nagg] It's a 100-story tower.
Eighty floors above ground, 20 below.

17:53.542 --> 17:54.750
Comms are still down.

17:54.833 --> 17:56.625
Damage report still coming in.

17:56.708 --> 17:59.417
I'm worried about the gas lines, fires.

17:59.500 --> 18:02.792
I'm also worried about the fuel source
on the ship, that it's unstable.

18:02.875 --> 18:04.292
[Slightly and Smee grunting]

18:04.375 --> 18:06.208
The ammunition, insecure.

18:06.917 --> 18:08.667
Don't get me started on radiation.

18:10.083 --> 18:13.167
They promised us reinforcements
from the city three hours ago,

18:13.750 --> 18:15.250
and all I see is you seven.

18:15.333 --> 18:18.042
[Kirsh] We're a special unit
here under orders from the founder.

18:18.125 --> 18:19.292
[Nagg] What kind of orders?

18:20.042 --> 18:21.333
You don't need to know that.

18:24.167 --> 18:25.333
[Ops Hamm] Hey.

18:25.417 --> 18:26.500
Chief.

18:27.500 --> 18:31.083
-What is she doing?
-You have a medic in your unit? Hermit?

18:31.167 --> 18:33.333
[Ops Hamm] He's on Rashidi's team.
They haven't checked in.

18:33.417 --> 18:35.542
Benjamin Rashidi, 32, sergeant.

18:37.000 --> 18:38.292
What is she doing?

18:46.875 --> 18:48.000
What floor is this?

18:48.750 --> 18:50.250
What floor is this?

18:51.958 --> 18:52.958
[Ops Hamm] Sixty-five.

18:57.875 --> 19:00.375
Wendy? Wendy.

19:00.458 --> 19:01.667
Slightly,

19:02.583 --> 19:04.000
go with her.

19:04.083 --> 19:06.250
-Me?
-The rest of you on me.

19:06.333 --> 19:07.375
We're moving fast.

19:07.458 --> 19:09.458
Assess the damage, rescue survivors.

19:09.542 --> 19:11.625
I want GPS on wounded
reported back to command.

19:25.958 --> 19:27.708
[newscaster on monitor
speaks indistinctly]

19:27.792 --> 19:29.667
…more medics are en route now.

19:29.750 --> 19:32.417
As we get updates,
we'll be letting you know.

19:33.000 --> 19:36.000
Emergency response are scanning
for life signs, but no…

19:36.583 --> 19:37.583
[chuckles]

19:40.917 --> 19:44.708
[sighs, chuckles] They're down.

19:44.792 --> 19:45.917
Data's pouring in.

19:47.167 --> 19:49.292
Feels like Christmas.

19:49.375 --> 19:52.167
Sir, I have Yutani on the line.

19:55.875 --> 19:58.292
[sighs]

19:58.375 --> 19:59.458
[beeps]

20:00.500 --> 20:02.750
It's been a very expensive day.

20:03.333 --> 20:04.333
Yeah, you're telling me.

20:04.917 --> 20:06.292
Not to mention lives lost.

20:06.375 --> 20:07.375
Of course.

20:08.167 --> 20:10.625
You have something that belongs to me.

20:10.708 --> 20:15.750
Uh, to be fair, it fell from the sky
and broke one of my buildings.

20:15.833 --> 20:18.458
Reparations will be made.
Just send us a bill.

20:19.208 --> 20:22.250
My men are on site now securing the crash.

20:23.833 --> 20:27.750
Is there anything we need to know, uh,
about the ship?

20:29.083 --> 20:31.083
A deep space research vessel.

20:31.167 --> 20:35.625
It goes without saying that everything
on board should be considered proprietary.

20:36.625 --> 20:38.708
I'd like permission to send a team.

20:38.792 --> 20:41.458
To secure the ship and remove what's ours.

20:41.958 --> 20:45.208
I'm… um, I'm afraid
I can't allow that just yet.

20:45.292 --> 20:48.583
You know that the, um,
tower is still too unstable.

20:49.375 --> 20:51.750
And I'm afraid I must insist.

20:51.833 --> 20:55.583
Um, I don't have to remind
you that… [sighs]

20:55.667 --> 21:01.208
…any incursion onto Prodigy territory
will be construed as a hostile act.

21:01.792 --> 21:03.917
This is what lawyers are for.

21:04.000 --> 21:07.417
You know, you have yours talk to mine,

21:08.375 --> 21:10.875
and then we'll negotiate
a treaty. [chuckles]

21:10.958 --> 21:12.833
Now, excuse me. I'm needed elsewhere.

21:17.958 --> 21:19.292
Predictable.

21:22.292 --> 21:23.917
I want what's on that ship.

21:27.125 --> 21:28.833
[chuckles]

21:30.583 --> 21:32.500
[electricity crackling]

21:44.500 --> 21:47.500
[garbled audio plays on speakers]

22:46.750 --> 22:49.375
[buzzing]

23:02.083 --> 23:03.375
[thinking] Something's here.

23:12.375 --> 23:13.875
I miss baths.

23:15.417 --> 23:18.125
I used to hate baths, but now I miss them.

23:18.208 --> 23:19.333
Quiet now.

23:21.292 --> 23:22.792
[chirping]

23:26.708 --> 23:28.417
Fear is for animals.

23:28.500 --> 23:29.792
You are not animals.

23:29.875 --> 23:30.917
Now move.

23:36.583 --> 23:38.000
[ship creaking]

23:38.083 --> 23:41.583
[clicking sound]

23:47.083 --> 23:49.375
-Fascinating.
-I want to go home now.

23:49.958 --> 23:51.083
It looks like a plant.

23:52.750 --> 23:54.083
It's a monster. Let's kill it.

23:55.000 --> 23:56.833
Scientists don't kill.

23:58.500 --> 24:03.042
Careful.
This is a non-terrestrial species.

24:03.125 --> 24:05.000
[Kirsh] We don't know
what it's capable of.

24:10.292 --> 24:11.917
[Boy Kavalier chuckles, grunts]

24:17.958 --> 24:19.917
Curly, you're on point.

24:20.542 --> 24:26.750
Take Smee and Nibs and see if you can find
something to capture it with.

24:45.375 --> 24:46.667
[Curly] Nibs, don't look.

24:47.375 --> 24:48.625
Yo, what is that?

24:49.958 --> 24:53.750
[squelching]

24:58.792 --> 25:00.000
[creature squeals]

25:02.292 --> 25:04.375
Ah. Monster.

25:05.125 --> 25:06.333
[whimpers]

25:06.833 --> 25:09.042
-Monster. M-Monsters! [whimpers]
-[Nibs whimpers]

25:10.917 --> 25:12.833
We should…
Weren't we supposed to catch it?

25:12.917 --> 25:15.917
-[Smee whimpers] Wait, was that blood?
-[glass shatters]

25:18.542 --> 25:20.333
Uh, there's more.

25:23.625 --> 25:25.250
[Smee] Whoa. Gross.

25:26.792 --> 25:27.792
[Nibs] Ugh…

25:47.042 --> 25:49.125
[purrs]

25:49.208 --> 25:51.292
[growls]

25:54.583 --> 25:56.000
[meows]

25:56.083 --> 25:57.750
[squawks, screeches softly]

25:58.708 --> 26:00.833
[growling, grunting]

26:12.750 --> 26:16.375
-[Smee whimpering] No! No!
-[Curly] Hey! Hey! [shrieks]

26:19.750 --> 26:21.917
[gasps, grunts]

26:24.000 --> 26:26.292
-Hey! Hey!
-[screaming]

26:26.375 --> 26:28.292
-[Curly] Throw it down!
-[Nibs shrieks]

26:28.375 --> 26:29.833
Nibs, please, please, please.

26:30.708 --> 26:32.708
-Oh!
-[clattering]

26:33.958 --> 26:34.958
[exhales]

27:07.000 --> 27:08.125
What is that?

27:09.125 --> 27:10.583
[squeaks]

27:14.042 --> 27:15.250
He was this way.

27:15.917 --> 27:17.000
Yuck!

27:18.542 --> 27:20.083
-Ugh.
-Are those…

27:21.792 --> 27:23.042
Are those scratches?

27:25.208 --> 27:26.417
Like fingernails?

27:26.500 --> 27:27.708
Like claws.

27:30.875 --> 27:32.042
Bear claws.

27:33.583 --> 27:36.333
Wait. There are bears?

27:39.667 --> 27:41.083
[radio static]

27:41.167 --> 27:45.208
This is Prodigy medic Hermit.
Come in. [breathing heavily]

27:45.292 --> 27:47.208
Rashidi, Siberian.

27:48.375 --> 27:49.625
Does anybody read me?

28:04.708 --> 28:06.000
Bergerfeld.

28:06.958 --> 28:09.917
Where the fuck is everybody?
Comms are down.

28:10.000 --> 28:12.250
This whole building feels
like it's about to collapse.

28:12.333 --> 28:14.125
Have you seen any animals?

28:14.208 --> 28:17.167
-Animals? What sort of animals?
-Like, uh, big animals.

28:17.250 --> 28:18.500
Like pets?

28:19.500 --> 28:21.125
No, definitely not like pets.

28:21.208 --> 28:23.500
[people laughing]

28:23.583 --> 28:25.833
I've cleared all the other apartments
on this floor.

28:25.917 --> 28:27.208
[Hermit grunts, breathes heavily]

28:28.000 --> 28:29.417
[Hermit] Search and rescue!

28:30.000 --> 28:32.167
[Bergerfeld] Security services! Open up!

28:33.292 --> 28:35.375
[laughing continues]

28:35.458 --> 28:38.583
[British accent] The noise. So much noise.

28:38.667 --> 28:40.583
Sir, we're evacuating the building.

28:40.667 --> 28:43.417
Please find the nearest elevator
and head down.

28:43.500 --> 28:46.542
We're having a dinner party.
The Caspians are here.

28:46.625 --> 28:49.583
There's a spaceship in the lobby.

28:49.667 --> 28:51.458
I think the Caspians will understand.

28:51.542 --> 28:56.875
Well, I'm sure if it's a real problem,
Boy Kavalier will call me personally.

28:57.542 --> 28:59.083
We belong to the same club.

28:59.167 --> 29:02.333
Well, sir, I don't know about that.

29:02.417 --> 29:04.542
I do know that the north stairwell is out

29:04.625 --> 29:06.708
and that the fire suppression system
is down,

29:06.792 --> 29:08.750
and until we can check
the structure of the building--

29:20.792 --> 29:21.833
Sir!

29:21.917 --> 29:24.250
[pounding on door]

29:24.333 --> 29:25.375
Sir!

29:27.833 --> 29:28.833
Move.

29:30.583 --> 29:32.250
[heavy footsteps]

29:34.167 --> 29:39.083
[hissing]

29:43.208 --> 29:45.708
-[creature screeches]
-[rapid gunfire]

29:47.958 --> 29:49.042
What the--

29:49.833 --> 29:52.375
Oh, my dear! [screaming]

29:55.458 --> 29:57.167
-[screams]
-[screeches]

29:57.250 --> 29:58.458
[grunts]

29:58.542 --> 30:03.833
[His Lordship and guests screaming]

30:05.917 --> 30:08.542
[grunts, pants]

30:08.625 --> 30:10.542
-[creature shrieking]
-[screaming]

30:13.792 --> 30:15.083
-[person screams]
-[body thuds]

30:15.667 --> 30:17.333
[panting]

30:17.417 --> 30:19.333
[creature hisses]

30:19.417 --> 30:21.833
[panting]

30:30.750 --> 30:34.750
[helicopter passing]

30:44.250 --> 30:47.208
[wind whistling]

31:00.750 --> 31:05.125
[His Lordship] The noise… noise…
So much noise.

31:08.583 --> 31:09.875
[grunts]

31:12.333 --> 31:14.667
[muttering] So much noise.

31:30.833 --> 31:34.000
[Hermit grunting]

31:34.083 --> 31:35.708
[creature shrieks]

31:36.667 --> 31:40.000
[screaming]

31:40.083 --> 31:41.417
[hissing]

31:41.500 --> 31:44.125
[screaming]

31:45.917 --> 31:48.500
[screeches]

31:53.583 --> 31:54.583
[Hermit panting]

31:56.333 --> 31:58.792
[panting]

32:12.167 --> 32:13.167
[Hermit grunts]

32:14.292 --> 32:15.708
Thank you.

32:32.792 --> 32:33.833
[weapon clicks]

33:18.500 --> 33:20.583
[fluid dripping]

33:20.667 --> 33:22.750
[chirping]

33:29.542 --> 33:32.542
It presents as flora, but it may be fauna.

33:37.167 --> 33:41.083
[Smee] Kirsh. Kirsh?

33:42.917 --> 33:44.000
Stay here.

33:45.417 --> 33:46.708
Keep an eye on this.

33:49.250 --> 33:50.542
[Smee] Kirsh?

33:57.792 --> 33:58.792
[Smee] Kirsh!

34:04.083 --> 34:06.500
Uh, it was… it was in the cat.

34:09.083 --> 34:10.458
What was in the cat?

34:14.500 --> 34:15.500
[Nibs] Don't!

34:16.708 --> 34:17.708
It's fast.

34:18.500 --> 34:20.333
[computer beeps]

34:35.792 --> 34:37.667
[Curly] It's like a zoo,
but the animals got out.

34:50.292 --> 34:51.417
[sighs]

35:10.000 --> 35:11.667
It's a research vessel.

35:11.750 --> 35:12.792
Deep space model.

35:13.917 --> 35:15.708
They must have been collecting specimens.

35:16.667 --> 35:18.667
[stammers] I thought
specimens meant "dead."

35:23.958 --> 35:25.125
[elevator bell dings]

35:27.875 --> 35:31.667
[Morrow grunting]

35:39.708 --> 35:40.792
[radio chatter]

35:40.875 --> 35:43.167
[Cortez] Sir, you need
to leave the building now.

35:43.917 --> 35:45.833
The stairs are blocked,
so I thought I could--

35:45.917 --> 35:48.167
There's been a crash.
Everyone has to go now.

35:48.750 --> 35:49.958
Of course.

35:50.042 --> 35:52.083
-I just need to know which way--
-[Brahma] What's in the bag?

35:53.167 --> 35:54.333
Supplies.

35:56.375 --> 35:57.792
-What the fuck?
-Hands!

35:59.792 --> 36:02.417
-Just calm down.
-Hands. Now!

36:09.792 --> 36:10.958
You're making a mistake.

36:11.458 --> 36:13.500
[Brahma] Shit. He's a cyborg.

36:13.583 --> 36:15.417
Don't move. Don't blink.

36:17.042 --> 36:18.042
Damn.

36:18.833 --> 36:21.583
Just stay calm, friend.
They can sense fear.

36:21.667 --> 36:22.917
[Cortez] I'm not your friend.

36:23.417 --> 36:25.458
[Brahma] Put your hands behind your back.

36:25.958 --> 36:28.292
And lock your fingers together now.

36:30.625 --> 36:33.958
Just so you know,
I'm the least of your problems.

36:41.625 --> 36:43.792
-[gunfire]
-[soldiers screaming]

36:43.875 --> 36:46.167
[bodies thudding]

36:48.500 --> 36:52.667
[hissing]

36:57.625 --> 37:00.625
-[hisses]
-[soldier] What the fuck is that?

37:00.708 --> 37:03.250
-[heavy footsteps]
-[soldier] Fuck! Move!

37:03.333 --> 37:05.167
-[heavy running footsteps]
-[soldier] Fuck!

37:05.250 --> 37:07.250
-[soldiers screaming]
-[creature roars]

37:07.333 --> 37:09.000
-Open fire!
-[rapid gunfire]

37:09.083 --> 37:13.167
-[soldiers groaning]
-[creature screeches]

37:18.208 --> 37:19.208
[gasps]

37:25.542 --> 37:26.750
[blade scraping]

37:53.500 --> 37:57.000
[Curly whispers] Hey! Psst.

37:57.083 --> 37:58.083
No, now.

37:59.375 --> 38:00.375
Come on.

38:23.667 --> 38:25.417
-Smee.
-Uh-huh?

38:25.500 --> 38:26.708
I need you there.

38:27.208 --> 38:28.542
You'll link up with Wendy.

38:28.625 --> 38:32.208
Secure the area. Nobody gets in or out
until the hazmat team arrives.

38:35.042 --> 38:36.208
O-Okay.

38:56.417 --> 38:57.708
Whoa.

39:05.792 --> 39:06.792
There is a bear.

39:12.792 --> 39:15.333
-Why?
-Warrior mode.

39:15.417 --> 39:16.500
Ugh.

39:20.500 --> 39:25.292
[young Hermit, Frank] ♪You've got to
Ac-cent-tchu-ate the positive ♪

39:25.375 --> 39:29.250
♪ And e-lim-i-nate the negative ♪

39:29.333 --> 39:33.875
♪ And latch on to the affirmative ♪

39:33.958 --> 39:35.583
♪ But don't mess with… ♪

39:35.667 --> 39:37.833
[breathes heavily]

39:41.583 --> 39:43.542
[grunts]

40:20.333 --> 40:21.333
[machine clicks]

40:21.417 --> 40:23.042
[crowd cheering]

40:23.125 --> 40:25.500
-Reggie Jackson has seen two pitches…
-Wow.

40:25.583 --> 40:26.958
…in the strike zone tonight.

40:27.042 --> 40:30.000
-Two. And he's hit 'em both in the seats.
-[crowd cheering]

40:33.583 --> 40:34.833
Would you look at that, Dad?

40:36.708 --> 40:41.833
Reggie Jackson, game six,
1977 World Series.

40:43.417 --> 40:46.542
New York Yankees
versus Los Angeles Dodgers.

40:46.625 --> 40:48.500
Reggie Jackson hits three home runs.

40:48.583 --> 40:51.542
-[crowd roars]
-[announcer 1] High and…

40:51.625 --> 40:53.417
-[announcer 2] Goodbye!
-[announcer 3] Goodbye!

40:54.667 --> 40:56.167
[announcer 3] Oh, what a blow!

40:56.667 --> 40:58.667
What a way to top it off!

40:59.167 --> 41:03.167
Forget about who the most
valuable player is in the World Series.

41:04.042 --> 41:06.875
How this man has responded to pressure.

41:08.042 --> 41:10.083
Oh, what a beam on his face.

41:10.167 --> 41:11.500
How can you blame him?

41:11.583 --> 41:13.417
He's answered the whole world.

41:13.500 --> 41:14.875
What are the odds?

41:16.917 --> 41:19.167
[announcer 3]
What a colossal [garbled] blow…

41:22.208 --> 41:24.583
[chuckles]

41:27.083 --> 41:28.542
Who are you talking to?

41:33.125 --> 41:34.167
My dad.

41:36.417 --> 41:37.667
You're hurt.

41:38.750 --> 41:40.208
-[Slightly] Me?
-Let me see.

41:42.042 --> 41:43.542
You talk to Dad?

41:44.042 --> 41:47.167
Uh, well, I know he's not… he's not here.

41:48.500 --> 41:49.750
-But, um…
-[sprayer bottle spritzing]

41:49.833 --> 41:53.500
You see this ball and the game…

41:54.167 --> 41:56.583
We used to watch
the old highlight reels together.

41:56.667 --> 41:58.042
He called it proof.

42:00.333 --> 42:03.417
He said sometimes the world
gives you a moment to shine.

42:05.792 --> 42:07.917
And if you do, well…

42:09.667 --> 42:13.375
There's a name for that kind of hero.

42:17.625 --> 42:20.208
He called him Mr. October.

42:21.542 --> 42:22.750
[chuckles] Mister?

42:23.375 --> 42:24.500
Where's the cut?

42:25.042 --> 42:26.042
[Slightly] There's no cut.

42:27.542 --> 42:30.083
There's a bear.
He ate the men in the hall.

42:30.167 --> 42:31.500
-A bear? [laughs]
-Mm-hmm.

42:31.583 --> 42:32.958
We don't bleed anyway.

42:33.625 --> 42:34.625
Not red anymore.

42:35.292 --> 42:37.500
-Uh…
-It's all white inside.

42:38.125 --> 42:41.417
-You're synthetic.
-Oh, we don't like that word.

42:41.500 --> 42:42.500
You're both synthetic.

42:42.583 --> 42:43.583
No, we're…

42:44.708 --> 42:47.042
-something different.
-Something special.

42:49.083 --> 42:51.292
-[Kirsh] Wendy?
-Yeah, Kirsh, we're here.

42:51.792 --> 42:53.750
We, um… [laughs] …we found him.

42:53.833 --> 42:55.417
I don't care about that.

42:55.500 --> 42:57.375
I need you to get to
the front section of the ship.

42:57.458 --> 42:59.958
-There's cargo I need you to secure.
-Um… [stammers]

43:00.042 --> 43:01.208
[Kirsh] Smee is already en route.

43:01.292 --> 43:02.292
Can it wait?

43:02.375 --> 43:05.250
Can it… No, it can't wait.

43:05.750 --> 43:07.250
These are invasive species.

43:07.333 --> 43:10.417
If we don't lock them down,
they could escape, breed.

43:10.958 --> 43:12.542
And then it will be too late.

43:12.625 --> 43:14.708
We should go.
Smee doesn't like being alone.

43:14.792 --> 43:17.167
-[Kirsh] Stop acting like children.
-[groans]

43:17.250 --> 43:19.250
-[Kirsh] Lives are at stake.
-We're not children anymore.

43:19.333 --> 43:20.708
[Kirsh] You need to go, now.

43:20.792 --> 43:21.875
Will you come with us?

43:21.958 --> 43:24.042
[stammers] I've got to get back.

43:24.125 --> 43:27.667
There will be loads of people there,
bloody, wounded, exploded.

43:27.750 --> 43:28.917
We're going to the front section.

43:32.250 --> 43:33.250
Please?

43:37.375 --> 43:38.667
Okay.

43:38.750 --> 43:39.750
Wendy…

43:41.375 --> 43:42.708
Yeah, okay. I…

43:44.375 --> 43:46.500
Keep up. We move fast.

43:53.542 --> 43:55.542
-[elevator bell dings]
-[electricity crackling]

44:07.875 --> 44:08.875
This way.

44:27.250 --> 44:28.250
[bell dings]

44:29.250 --> 44:31.292
[creature hissing]

44:43.792 --> 44:44.792
Excuse me.

44:51.250 --> 44:53.208
What did he mean
you're not children anymore?

44:54.042 --> 44:55.167
Uh, we are kids.

44:56.208 --> 44:57.917
What… I don't get it.

44:58.000 --> 45:00.625
-I'm 11, and Wendy just turned 12.
-Slightly.

45:00.708 --> 45:02.083
That's you? Your name's Wendy?

45:02.167 --> 45:03.250
No, that's her machine name.

45:03.333 --> 45:05.167
When we were children,
we fell really sick.

45:05.250 --> 45:08.583
Then we were given these big bodies, but
my name's actually Aarush and she's Marcy.

45:08.667 --> 45:10.292
My sister's name is Marcy.

45:11.542 --> 45:12.833
-Dude.
-Don't you dare.

45:13.542 --> 45:16.667
-That's your sister.
-Slightly, secret. Go.

45:16.750 --> 45:19.083
-You weren't telling him.
-Go. Get up there, now.

45:20.417 --> 45:21.417
[sighs]

45:32.917 --> 45:34.000
Joe.

45:37.208 --> 45:38.208
[Wendy chuckles]

45:39.167 --> 45:40.167
It's me.

45:42.250 --> 45:43.417
I found you.

45:46.875 --> 45:51.167
I-I've been watching you
all the time on the screens.

45:51.250 --> 45:54.708
I watch you go to work,
I watch you ride in boats.

45:55.833 --> 45:57.042
You help people.

45:59.083 --> 46:00.958
Face my fury.

46:03.417 --> 46:04.500
You remember?

46:06.625 --> 46:08.000
And I'm sorry. It is my fault.

46:08.083 --> 46:09.833
You wanted to go to Mars.

46:09.917 --> 46:11.917
-And I couldn't… I wouldn't…
-No, no, no.

46:12.000 --> 46:13.250
You died.

46:15.542 --> 46:17.000
I went to the funeral.

46:18.375 --> 46:19.417
No. Daddy…

46:22.458 --> 46:23.625
Daddy said…

46:26.375 --> 46:29.167
Joe, when I was sick,
the boy genius came to visit me.

46:29.958 --> 46:33.417
And he told Daddy that he could help me,
but I had to go away.

46:34.583 --> 46:37.583
So they took me to live
with Kirsh and Dame Sylvia.

46:37.667 --> 46:38.667
I don't understand.

46:38.750 --> 46:39.958
But that was the way.

46:41.417 --> 46:43.250
-Joe.
-[sniffs]

46:43.333 --> 46:44.417
Or I would die.

46:47.542 --> 46:48.792
They said I was special.

46:51.750 --> 46:52.875
Dad told me--

46:52.958 --> 46:54.708
Daddy said don't talk.

46:56.667 --> 46:58.583
[whispers] Daddy said
it had to be a secret.

47:02.042 --> 47:03.292
They said I would be okay.

47:05.583 --> 47:06.875
But I could never go home.

47:08.792 --> 47:10.792
-Who said?
-The boy genius.

47:12.458 --> 47:13.958
His name is on your uniform.

47:16.875 --> 47:18.958
[Slightly] Guys, Kirsh said we gotta go.

47:24.667 --> 47:25.792
Please.

48:03.625 --> 48:05.708
[buzzing]

48:22.417 --> 48:24.500
-Think it's inside.
-Your first day of day care.

48:24.583 --> 48:25.583
Dad picked you up.

48:25.667 --> 48:27.708
You were filthy and your lip was bleeding.

48:27.792 --> 48:28.833
What did you say?

48:30.125 --> 48:31.667
I am mad to them.

48:35.000 --> 48:38.042
-Let me. [grunts]
-[metal scrapes]

48:42.208 --> 48:43.250
I could have done that.

48:46.208 --> 48:47.208
Christmas morning.

48:47.958 --> 48:48.958
You were seven.

48:50.625 --> 48:52.208
You woke me up before the sun.

48:56.083 --> 48:57.083
What did you say?

49:00.125 --> 49:03.417
I still don't think my big toe
looks like my thumb.

49:27.542 --> 49:28.542
[Hermit sighs]

49:29.125 --> 49:31.292
[Slightly] Uh, guys?

49:42.250 --> 49:43.458
[buzzing]

49:50.292 --> 49:52.292
[buzzing continues]

50:11.458 --> 50:13.708
-[buzzing]
-Do you hear that?

50:20.542 --> 50:23.667
I hear the sound of metal bending
like the ship's about to fall.

50:23.750 --> 50:25.625
[creature screeching]

50:32.708 --> 50:35.875
[buzzing]

50:54.125 --> 50:55.583
[distant screeching]

51:00.583 --> 51:01.583
Call it in.

51:01.667 --> 51:03.250
Hmm. Looks like eggs.

51:03.333 --> 51:06.000
And then I think…

51:08.917 --> 51:11.125
-No!
-[Hermit screams]

51:11.208 --> 51:12.500
Joe!

51:16.042 --> 51:17.208
Slightly?

51:17.292 --> 51:19.458
-Should we jump?
-Slightly. Slightly!

51:19.542 --> 51:20.542
Stay here.

51:20.625 --> 51:22.500
Look at me. Stay safe.

51:22.583 --> 51:23.875
-No.
-Guard the omelet.

51:23.958 --> 51:25.333
No, no, no. Wendy!

51:25.417 --> 51:27.417
[♪ "Stinkfist" playing]

51:37.208 --> 51:39.875
♪ Something has to change ♪

51:39.958 --> 51:42.667
♪ Undeniable dilemma ♪

51:42.750 --> 51:47.125
♪ Boredom's not a burden
Anyone should bear ♪

51:47.208 --> 51:50.667
♪ Just not enough, I need more ♪

51:50.750 --> 51:52.583
♪ Nothing seems to satisfy ♪

51:52.667 --> 51:56.000
♪ I said, I don't want it
I just need it ♪

51:56.583 --> 51:59.750
♪ To breathe, to feel, to know I'm alive ♪

52:02.958 --> 52:06.167
♪ Finger deep within the borderline ♪

52:06.750 --> 52:10.292
♪ Show me that you love me
And that we belong together ♪

52:10.875 --> 52:16.417
♪ Relax, turn around and take my hand ♪

52:26.500 --> 52:30.417
♪ I can help you change ♪

52:30.500 --> 52:33.167
♪ Tired moments into pleasure ♪

52:33.250 --> 52:38.958
♪ Say the word and we'll be
Well upon our way ♪

52:39.042 --> 52:43.250
♪ Blend and balance, pain and comfort ♪

52:43.333 --> 52:48.667
♪ Deep within you
Till you will not want me any other way ♪

52:49.250 --> 52:52.625
♪ But it's not enough, I need more ♪

52:52.708 --> 52:54.625
♪ Nothing seems to satisfy ♪

52:54.708 --> 52:57.875
♪ I said, I don't want it
I just need it ♪

52:58.458 --> 53:01.583
♪ To breathe, to feel, to know I'm alive ♪

53:04.667 --> 53:07.958
♪ Elbow deep inside the borderline ♪

53:08.542 --> 53:12.625
♪ Show me that you love me
And that we belong together ♪

53:12.708 --> 53:15.792
♪ Shoulder deep within the borderline ♪

53:16.750 --> 53:22.417
♪ Relax, turn around and take my hand ♪

53:31.500 --> 53:33.500
[song ends]

54:51.583 --> 54:52.583
-[heart beats]
-[gun fires]

54:52.667 --> 54:53.750
[rocket engine roars]
